Third-party code incorporated in CafAI
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Crema (https://github.com/yarneo/crema), GPL-3.0
  Copyright (C) 2026 Yarden (yarneo). Licensed GPLv3 (GPL-3.0-only).
  CafAI ports non-UI logic from Crema's web/ folder (commit
  628cd714fa1a3a5194ea0e4c579d54ae1e38353c): the Decaid gateway client and
  WebSocket handling, profile handling and required-field fixes, shot curve
  analysis, provider calls, settings mirroring, safe-area handling, the
  dev/ipad.html device harness and release tooling, together with the tests
  that cover them. Each ported file carries a header naming its Crema origin
  and stating that it was modified for CafAI. See docs/CREMA_PORT_PLAN.md.

MimojaCafe skin for de1app, GPL-3.0
  Crema began as a fork of the MimojaCafe de1app skin; parts of Crema's web/
  logic were ported from that Tcl lineage. CafAI credits it accordingly.

Decent Espresso profiles (https://github.com/decentespresso/decaid)
  The coach templates in src/coach/templates/source/ are bundled Decent
  profiles copied from Decaid's assets/defaultProfiles. See SOURCES.md in that
  folder for exact origins and licensing.

Decaid's API specs and agent docs (https://github.com/decentespresso/decaid)
  Copyright (C) 2025-2026 Decent Espresso. Licensed GPL-3.0-or-later.
  contract/decaid/spec/ holds Decaid's assets/api specs, contract/decaid/skill/
  its agent skill (.agents/skills/decent-app/) and contract/decaid/doc/ its
  API notes (doc/AI_API_NOTES.md), verbatim at the commit in
  contract/decaid/PIN.json. CafAI's checks and coding agents read them; none
  of them is part of the app or its release zip.

